bots: a trade request reaches the bot (trade.rs2)

Progressive's bot hunks: when a player asks a bot to trade, the bot is told (stage 0); when a trade
window of a bot closes, its trade state is reset (stage -1).
Not carried over: Progressive's trailing-whitespace fix on the duel-arena `return;`, and its
`.say("One moment please, <displayname>")` in [opplayer4,_]: every bot said it, also one whose task
cannot trade. The bot library answers instead (BotTrade.onTradeRequest: it takes the request or
declines).

diff --git a/scripts/interface_trade/scripts/trade.rs2 b/scripts/interface_trade/scripts/trade.rs2
index cc38e00..37a9acc 100644
--- a/scripts/interface_trade/scripts/trade.rs2
+++ b/scripts/interface_trade/scripts/trade.rs2
@@ -32,6 +32,9 @@ if (.busy = true) {
     mes("<.displayname> is busy at the moment.");
     return;
 }
+if(.p_isbot = 1) {
+    .p_bot_interact_trade(uid, 0); //Begin (stage 0)
+}
 
 // this message always sends, even if this player is responding to a trade request
 mes("Sending trade offer...");
@@ -241,12 +244,18 @@ while ($slot < .inv_size($inv)) {
 inv_stoptransmit(trademain:inv);
 inv_stoptransmit(trademain:otherinv);
 inv_stoptransmit(tradeside:inv);
+if(p_isbot = 1) {
+    p_bot_interact_trade(null, -1); //reset
+}
 
 ~moveallinv(tradeoffer, inv);
 
 if (.finduid(%tradepartner) = true) {
     .%tradepartner = null;
     .if_close;
+    if(.p_isbot = 1) {
+        .p_bot_interact_trade(null, -1); //reset
+    }
     if (%tradestatus ! 1 & .%tradestatus ! 1) {
         .mes("Other player declined trade."); // osrs
     }
